<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Login page branding — THEME_PLAN §3.3, §15.2 B9.

    §3.3 deleted Aura's login_templates.xml and let the page fall back to stock
    Odoo, on the reasoning that a half-styled custom login is worse than a plain
    one.  That was the right call at the time; this file is the rebrand it was
    waiting for.  Note the filename deliberately matches the one that was
    deleted — same job, now owned by the module that owns the visual layer.

    ⚠ WHY A TEMPLATE OVERRIDE AND NOT res.company.logo.
    Setting the company logo would be the broader fix — it also reaches reports,
    portal pages and outgoing mail.  It is NOT used here because res.company.logo
    is `related='partner_id.image_1920'`, an Image field: Odoo generates resized
    variants of it through PIL, which does not rasterise SVG.  Storing an SVG
    there works until something asks for image_128 and then fails in a place far
    away from this change.  If the logo is ever wanted on reports and mail too,
    supply a PNG for the company field and keep this template for the crisp
    vector on screen.
-->
<odoo>
    <template id="login_layout_brand" inherit_id="web.login_layout">
        <!--
            Stock markup (web/views/webclient_templates.xml:121):

              <img t-attf-src="/web/binary/company_logo{{ '?dbname='+db if db else '' }}"
                   alt="Logo" style="max-height:120px; max-width: 100%; width:auto"/>

            /web/binary/company_logo serves Odoo's "Your logo" placeholder when
            no company logo is set, which is what the demo was showing.  The
            dbname query param is dropped with it — irrelevant for a static file.
        -->
        <!--
            ⚠ Anchored on the wrapper's CLASS, not on the img's attributes.
            The obvious `//img[@alt='Logo']` is rejected outright by Odoo:

                View inheritance may not use attribute 'alt' as a selector.

            Odoo whitelists which attributes an inheritance xpath may select on,
            and `alt` is not among them — `class` is, through hasclass(). The
            logo's wrapper div (`text-center pb-3 border-bottom mb-4`) is the
            nearest legal anchor, and it holds exactly one img.
        -->
        <xpath expr="//div[hasclass('border-bottom')]/img" position="replace">
            <!--
                ⚠ The inline style is deliberate, and mirrors the stock markup it
                replaces.  logo_methode.svg carries width="700" height="700"
                attributes, so if this element ever renders before login.scss is
                available it would paint at 700px and blow the card apart.  The
                sizing constraint has to travel with the element, not live only
                in a stylesheet — this is the first screen a prospect sees.
                Refinements beyond "do not explode" belong in login.scss.
            -->
            <img src="/methode_theme/static/description/brand/logo_methode.svg"
                 alt="Méthode"
                 class="o_methode_login_logo"
                 style="max-height:120px; max-width: 100%; width:auto"/>
        </xpath>
    </template>
</odoo>
